<section class="transition-research">
  <div class="transition-research__container">
    
    <h2 class="transition-research__title">Published Research</h2>

    <div class="transition-research__category">
      <h3 class="transition-research__category-title">The Neurobiology of Waking</h3>

      <div class="transition-research__article-grid">
        <article class="transition-article-card">
          
          <h4 class="transition-article-card__title">
            <a href="/blogs/journal/how-your-prefrontal-cortex-boots-up">How Your Prefrontal Cortex Boots Up</a>
          </h4>

          <p class="transition-article-card__excerpt">
            Your executive function doesn't activate instantly. The prefrontal cortex needs specific signals to engage.
          </p>

          <div class="transition-article-card__meta">
            <span class="transition-article-card__reading-time">8 min read</span>
          </div>

          <a href="/blogs/journal/how-your-prefrontal-cortex-boots-up" class="transition-article-card__link">
            Read Article →
          </a>

        </article>

        <article class="transition-article-card">
          
          <h4 class="transition-article-card__title">
            <a href="/blogs/journal/arousal-vs-consciousness">Arousal vs. Consciousness: Why You're Not Fully Awake Yet</a>
          </h4>

          <p class="transition-article-card__excerpt">
            Being awake and being conscious are different neurological states. Understanding the gap changes how you approach mornings.
          </p>

          <div class="transition-article-card__meta">
            <span class="transition-article-card__reading-time">7 min read</span>
          </div>

          <a href="/blogs/journal/arousal-vs-consciousness" class="transition-article-card__link">
            Read Article →
          </a>

        </article>

        <article class="transition-article-card">
          
          <h4 class="transition-article-card__title">
            <a href="/blogs/journal/the-reticular-activating-system">The Reticular Activating System: Why the Transition Is Hard</a>
          </h4>

          <p class="transition-article-card__excerpt">
            Sleep inertia is real. Your brain's primary attention system needs time to reboot after sleep.
          </p>

          <div class="transition-article-card__meta">
            <span class="transition-article-card__reading-time">9 min read</span>
          </div>

          <a href="/blogs/journal/the-reticular-activating-system" class="transition-article-card__link">
            Read Article →
          </a>

        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="transition-research__category">
      <h3 class="transition-research__category-title">Circadian Timing & Morning Biology</h3>

      <div class="transition-research__article-grid">
        <article class="transition-article-card">
          
          <h4 class="transition-article-card__title">
            <a href="/blogs/journal/cortisol-timing-and-morning-activation">Cortisol Timing and Morning Activation</a>
          </h4>

          <p class="transition-article-card__excerpt">
            Cortisol naturally peaks upon waking. Understanding the rhythm lets you work with it instead of against it.
          </p>

          <div class="transition-article-card__meta">
            <span class="transition-article-card__reading-time">7 min read</span>
          </div>

          <a href="/blogs/journal/cortisol-timing-and-morning-activation" class="transition-article-card__link">
            Read Article →
          </a>

        </article>

        <article class="transition-article-card">
          
          <h4 class="transition-article-card__title">
            <a href="/blogs/journal/light-exposure-and-melatonin">Light Exposure and Melatonin Production: Why Dark Mornings Are Harder</a>
          </h4>

          <p class="transition-article-card__excerpt">
            The absence of light keeps melatonin elevated, extending sleep mode into waking hours. First light is critical.
          </p>

          <div class="transition-article-card__meta">
            <span class="transition-article-card__reading-time">8 min read</span>
          </div>

